A recommendation is a category-B-recommendation and is an evidence-type-4-recommendation.
If a clinician prescribes an initial-opioid-therapy for an acute-pain then the clinician should review a controlled-substance-prescription-history with a state-PDMP-record.
If a clinician prescribes an initial-opioid-therapy for a subacute-pain then the clinician should review a controlled-substance-prescription-history with a state-PDMP-record.
If a clinician prescribes an initial-opioid-therapy for a chronic-pain then the clinician should review a controlled-substance-prescription-history with a state-PDMP-record.
Every clinician should review a controlled-substance-prescription-history with a state-PDMP-record during a chronic-opioid-therapy.
Every clinician should assess an opioid-dosage for a high-overdose-risk and should assess a medication-combination for a high-overdose-risk.
